id: pm-gh1773
title: "GH-1773: refusal envelopes echo URL userinfo when it contains whitespace and a percent-encoded @ separator"
description: "GH-1773 (filed 2026-11-23 from the pm-rust parity review, reproduced on the pinned pm-cli oracle; native and TS behave the same). A refusal envelope echoes an open blocker's title verbatim. When that title holds a URL whose userinfo contains whitespace and a percent-encoded @ (https://fixture:fake words%40example.invalid/path), the userinfo is not masked: pm start-task sample-one --json refused by that blocker prints 'fixture:fake words'. Expected: credential-shaped URL userinfo is masked in every refusal and diagnostic projection, whitespace-bearing userinfo and an encoded separator included, matching the masking of plain user:pass@host; plain masking unchanged. Duplicate check: searched redaction URL userinfo whitespace percent-encoded separator refusal envelope; pm-gh1707 (closed) fixed public-URL @-in-path over-redaction and claim-refusal echoes, pm-nhauur and pm-5htunt (closed) cover other echo surfaces, none covers whitespace plus encoded separators."
type: Issue
status: in_progress
priority: 2
