comments[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-11-23T21:44:48.289Z","harness:claude-code","Root cause and fix (2026-11-23): redactUrlCredentialsInText judged each whitespace-delimited word alone, so a stored title holding a URL whose password contains a blank split into a scheme word with a colon but no at sign and a host word with an at sign (or its percent escape) but no colon; neither word matched the token rule. The plain at-sign form leaked the same way, not only the encoded one, and Node's WHATWG URL parser reads that spelling as userinfo with a spaced password. Fix in src/core/shared/url-credentials.ts: before the word rule, a word with no at sign that opens a URL authority with a user-colon prefix (scheme, one or two slashes, a colon that port digits alone never follow, no path, no bracketed IPv6 host) is joined across any whitespace with the later words up to the first that holds an at sign or its escape, within 16 words and 512 code units and before another URL starts, and the joined span goes through redactUrlCredentialsInToken. Line breaks and tabs count as blanks because URL parsers drop them. Host-and-port and plain-host prose before a later at sign stays intact. Every outbound surface (refusal guidance in JSON and text, telemetry sanitizeString, Sentry scrubbing) already routes free text through this one function. Verified end to end in a sandbox: a start-task refusal gated by such a blocker now prints the scheme, the placeholder and the host only, in JSON and TOON output."
